ters this year show Reed ahead by 18 to 20 points, most recently 53 to 33 in late September. Every major race rating, from the Cook Political Report to Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the contest in the safest Democratic column, and prediction markets price Reed's chances around 99 percent. An independent candidate has raised little and does not materially change the picture.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 18.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9957, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9974, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9952, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9973, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9965, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9977, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9986, "margin": 20.0}]}